  "id": "wf4-integrity-severity-tie-keeps-earlier-push",
  "description": "Two conflicts that carry the SAME severity code — two DUPLICATE_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY entries, one per duplicated key — must leave the EARLIER-pushed one as the headline: the ranking scan is strictly-less-than, so a tie never replaces `worst` and a rerun of the same snapshot names the same conflict. The reason string must still separate DISTINCT ambiguous actions (5 action_ids, read across both keys' rows) from conflict records (2).",
  "why_it_exists": "harness/FINDINGS.md section 1 fix: `if (severityRank(conflicts[i].code) < severityRank(worst.code)) worst = conflicts[i];` is deliberately strict so equal ranks keep the earlier push. Every other ranking scenario in the suite compares DIFFERENT ranks — wf4-integrity-severity-headlines-field-mismatch ranks DUPLICATE_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY (1) against DUPLICATE_ACTION_ID_FIELD_MISMATCH (0) and wf4-integrity-conflict-count-distinct-ids does the same pair — so none of them can prove what a same-rank tie does. This fixture pushes key 'MAT-20260101-010|004' first (spanning ids 004 and 005) and key 'MAT-20260101-010|006' second (spanning ids 006, 007 and 008): both rank 1, the first stays the headline, and the count reads five distinct ids reported as two records — a stricter distinct-vs-record split than any existing scenario.",
